--TEST--
a name written between the `<` and `>` of a type's arguments is a type, so no variable is offered there, read off the type name in front of the `<` because a `<` after a value compares, `rule:ide/completion-offers-only-what-the-compiler-derived`
--FILE--
<?nvs
namespace Shop;

class Money {}
var $money = new Money();

array<string, <|>
--REQUEST--
completion prefix=$
--EXPECT--
none
